# The published short links, and the two URL moves this site has made.
#
# These were `next.config.ts` `redirects()`, and before that a `_redirects` on the
# Cloudflare Pages site. They are back in the file Cloudflare reads directly:
# every one is a published URL — in the README, in the install instructions, on the
# socials — so they are part of the deployed contract, and a plain file is the one
# form where "what does /x do in production" is answerable by reading.
#
# 302 throughout, never 301. A 301 is cached by the browser more or less forever,
# every social link points at a third-party account that can move, and the docs
# have now moved origin twice in three days.
#
# `/install` is deliberately absent: it is a real script at `public/install`,
# served as a static asset. A redirect would break `curl -fsS` without `-L`.

/github         https://github.com/sigiroai              302
/x              https://x.com/SigiroAI                   302
/twitter        https://x.com/SigiroAI                   302
/linkedin       https://www.linkedin.com/company/sigiro  302
/discord        https://discord.gg/sigiro                302

# `@astrojs/sitemap` writes `sitemap-index.xml` and has no option to collapse it
# into one file, but `/sitemap.xml` is the path the old `robots.ts` declared and the
# one Search Console holds.
/sitemap.xml    /sitemap-index.xml                       302

# The docs are pages of this site again, at `/docs/*`, so almost the whole
# `/docs/*` block that used to live here is gone — those are native routes now and
# need no rule at all. What remains is the API reference, which was a page per
# operation under fumadocs and is one generated page now.
#
# Enumerated rather than matched, and that is not a style choice: with
# `/docs/api/*` Cloudflare appends the unmatched remainder to a destination that
# does not name `:splat`, and `/docs/api/:op` is not matched at all. Both were
# deployed, and both 404'd in production. The list is affordable because it is
# closed — these came from two generations of `fumadocs-openapi`, both deleted, and
# nothing can add a twelfth. Recovered with
# `git log --all --name-only -- 'www/content/docs/api/**' 'www/src/app/docs/api/**'`.
#
# The four `/admin/*` operations are absent on purpose. They no longer exist in the
# public spec — `/openapi.json` filters them — so there is no page to send anyone
# to, and a redirect would be the one place still advertising that they are there.
/docs/api/get-trace              /docs/api/     302
/docs/api/investigate-services   /docs/api/     302
/docs/api/list-anomalies         /docs/api/     302
/docs/api/list-services          /docs/api/     302
/docs/api/run-query              /docs/api/     302
/docs/api/v1/anomalies/get       /docs/api/     302
/docs/api/v1/investigate/post    /docs/api/     302
/docs/api/v1/query/post          /docs/api/     302
/docs/api/v1/services/get        /docs/api/     302
/docs/api/v1/traces/trace_id/get /docs/api/     302
